      "summary": "Pottery vessel in a jug form. Vessel has a vertical neck and does not feature a spout. Brown and unglazed. Flat base (with marks indicating potentially produced on a potter&#039;s wheel). Circular incised decoration on upper and mid body. A channel is seen around the vessel near the base. The handle features multiple channels along its length with two nubbins at its base, as well as a protrusion at the top of the handle where it connects with the vessel rim. This protrusion features a hole in it (for hanging?). There is a small hole in the base, seemingly produced before firing. The vessel has been refitted following breakage (half of vessel was broken).",
